# Firefox picks its idle inhibitor backend by auto-detection, and the first
# candidate -- FreeDesktopScreensaver -- always wins here because hypridle owns
# the org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver DBus name. That path is unreliable: hypridle
# only samples the inhibit count at the instant a timer fires, and Firefox drops
# and retakes its wakelock constantly during playback (ad breaks and MSE source
# switches leave it at zero locks for seconds at a time), so a windowed video
# blanks the screen whenever the 60s timer lands in one of those gaps.
# WaylandIdleInhibit uses zwp_idle_inhibit_manager_v1 instead, and Hyprland
# restarts the idle countdown when an inhibitor is released, so the flapping
# cannot expire it. Fullscreen was already covered by the idle_inhibit window
# rule in dot_config/hypr/config/windowrules.lua.
export MOZ_WAKE_LOCK_TYPE=WaylandIdleInhibit
